course: dictionary
lesson: 10564
title: Unclip and the clues of un-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are made from smaller parts, and the parts give clues. «Never touch or unclip a stranger's dog without the owner's permission.» Unclip is a verb. It means to open or remove a clip so that it comes loose or apart.
explain: Look at the start of the word. The un- means undo, and clip is the fastener. So unclip means undo a clip. Try it in the sentence: «Never touch or undo a stranger's dog's clip without permission.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: You unclip many things: a seatbelt, a bike helmet, or a dog's lead in the park. Only unclip your seatbelt after the car has stopped, because that is the safe time to do it.
fact: Unclip means to open or remove a clip so that it comes loose or apart.
fact: The un- at the start often means undo, so unclip means undo a clip.
fact: «Unclip the seatbelt» means open the clip, but only do it after the car has stopped.
fact: Unclip is a verb. Its forms are unclips, unclipped and unclipping.
fact: Clip is the fastening, and unclip is the opposite action of clip.
exercise: «Never touch or unclip a stranger's dog without the owner's permission.» What does unclip mean? | *Open the clip so the lead comes loose | Walk the dog home | Feed the dog a treat | Wash the dog's collar
exercise: Why should you unclip your seatbelt only after the car has stopped? | *Because it is safe to do it when the car is still | Because the car needs the belt to start | Because seatbelts only work at night | Because the seatbelt is too tight to open while driving
exercise: Find the word that means the opposite of unclip. | *clip | loosen | remove | open
test: «Unclip the seatbelt» means: | *Open the clip so the belt comes loose | Buy a new car | Tighten the belt | Hide the belt
test: Yesterday she ___ her bike helmet at the park. | unclipping | unclips | *unclipped | unclip
exam: Which is a safe time to unclip a seatbelt? | Before the car has stopped | At the start of the journey | While the car is moving fast | *Only after the car has stopped
